IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg4-s216-quorum-vote`

-- Tests of dg4-s216-quorum-vote.l4. Expected values are written by hand from the text of s 216
-- (de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, lines 811-818), beside each assertion, never copied from the module's own output.

§ `Tests of s 216`

§§ `The quorum`

-- src:813: absent a specification, a majority of the shares entitled to vote, present or by proxy, is a quorum (more than half)
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` NOTHING 100 51 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` NOTHING 100 50 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` NOTHING 100 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` NOTHING 100 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a specified quorum of 40 of 100: reaching it is enough
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` (JUST 40) 100 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` (JUST 40) 100 39 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a quorum may be set above a majority too
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` (JUST 75) 100 74 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` (JUST 75) 100 75 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- in no event less than 1/3: a specified 20 of 100 is floored at 1/3 (33.33...), so 33 is too few and 34 is enough
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` (JUST 20) 100 33 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` (JUST 20) 100 34 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- exactly 1/3 of 90 is 30
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` (JUST 20) 90 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` (JUST 20) 90 29 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- counts that cannot be a vote are not covered: no votes entitled, or more present than entitled
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` NOTHING 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` (JUST 40) 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` NOTHING 100 101 EQUALS NOTHING
-- a quorum for a class voting separately: the same floor of 1/3 of the shares of the class (class of 60 votes: 20)
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` (JUST 10) 60 20 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216 a quorum is present` (JUST 10) 60 19 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `The votes necessary for a matter other than the election of directors`

-- src:814: the majority of the shares present and entitled to vote on the subject matter is the act of the stockholders
-- arguments: the requirement, votes in favour, votes of the outstanding stock, votes present and entitled on the matter, votes cast
`t216 default requirement` MEANS `s 216 the vote that is necessary for a matter other than the election of directors` NOTHING NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 default requirement` 41 100 80 80 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 default requirement` 40 100 80 80 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the votes of the shares present, not of the outstanding shares, are the base
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 default requirement` 30 100 50 50 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the chapter requires a vote of a majority of the outstanding stock for the action: that vote, not the default
`t216 chapter requirement` MEANS `s 216 the vote that is necessary for a matter other than the election of directors` (JUST (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`)) NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 chapter requirement` 51 100 80 80 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 chapter requirement` 50 100 80 80 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the chapter's requirement beats a different one in the bylaws
`t216 chapter beats bylaws` MEANS `s 216 the vote that is necessary for a matter other than the election of directors` (JUST (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`)) (JUST (`a majority of` `the votes cast`))
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 chapter beats bylaws` 51 100 80 80 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 chapter beats bylaws` 50 100 80 80 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no chapter requirement: the bylaws' two-thirds of the votes cast (66 2/3% is 2/3 exactly): 2 of 3 reaches it, 66 of 100 does not
`t216 bylaws two thirds of votes cast` MEANS `s 216 the vote that is necessary for a matter other than the election of directors` NOTHING (JUST (`at least` ((200 DIVIDED BY 3)%) `of` `the votes cast`))
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 bylaws two thirds of votes cast` 2 100 80 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 bylaws two thirds of votes cast` 66 100 80 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 bylaws two thirds of votes cast` 67 100 80 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a base the section's rule does not size
`t216 odd base` MEANS `s 216 the vote that is necessary for a matter other than the election of directors` NOTHING (JUST (`a majority of` `the whole board`))
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 odd base` 5 100 80 80 EQUALS NOTHING
-- counts that cannot be a vote
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` `t216 default requirement` 5 100 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Directors are elected by a plurality`

-- src:815: one seat. 50 against 30 and 20 wins; 50 against 60 loses; 50 against 50 is a tie for the seat
#ASSERT `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` 50 (LIST 30, 20) 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` 50 (LIST 60) 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` 50 (LIST 50, 20) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- a plurality need not be a majority: 40 of 100 wins against 35 and 25
#ASSERT `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` 40 (LIST 35, 25) 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- two seats
#ASSERT `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` 45 (LIST 50, 40, 30) 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` 30 (LIST 50, 40, 20) 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` 40 (LIST 50, 40, 20, 30) 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` 40 (LIST 50, 30, 20) 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an unopposed candidate
#ASSERT `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` 0 EMPTY 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no seats to fill: not covered
#ASSERT `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` 50 (LIST 30) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 216(4): a separate vote by a class or series`

-- a majority of the outstanding shares of the class, present or by proxy, is a quorum entitled to act on that matter
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the class or series has a quorum entitled to take action on the matter` 100 51 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the class or series has a quorum entitled to take action on the matter` 100 50 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the class or series has a quorum entitled to take action on the matter` 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the act of the class: the majority of the shares of the class present at the meeting
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the matter is the act of the class or series` 60 31 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the matter is the act of the class or series` 60 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the matter is the act of the class or series` 60 61 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Closing sentence: the bylaw on the votes for the election of directors`

#ASSERT `s 216 the board of directors may further amend or repeal the bylaw amendment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a bylaw adopted by the board, or one that says nothing about director elections, is not what the sentence covers
#ASSERT `s 216 the board of directors may further amend or repeal the bylaw amendment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216 the board of directors may further amend or repeal the bylaw amendment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
